Falsifies `elf::verification::a_passing_check_has_no_address_overflow`.

The defect: the virtual-range check is deleted. It is the one line here whose value is thrown
away, so it reads as a statement with no effect, and the two checks above it already returned
everything the function computes. What it actually does is hand a guarantee forward: `validate`
and `page_range` both add `vaddr + memsz` unchecked because this line proved they can.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(vaddr.checked_add(memsz).is_some())`, on a segment
whose virtual range wraps, which is a crafted binary panicking the kernel in the code that
trusts this function.

diff --git a/crates/elf/src/lib.rs b/crates/elf/src/lib.rs
index 98694d352..f342f83b2 100644
--- a/crates/elf/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/elf/src/lib.rs
@@ -587,4 +587,2 @@ fn check_segment_bounds(
     // i.e. a crafted binary halting the kernel.
-    vaddr.checked_add(memsz).ok_or(Error::AddressOverflow)?;
-
     Ok(end)
